WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.870
Our classroom fan runs all afternoon,

2
00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:04.730
even when the room is empty.

3
00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:07.650
That wastes power and money.

4
00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:10.600
I want it on only when it's hot

5
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.360
and someone is in the room.

6
00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:14.750
That isn't a gadget problem.

7
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.060
It's a logic problem.

8
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:21.640
Today: logic, the switches that make

9
00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.000
decisions inside every device.

10
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.660
Inside a device, every signal

11
00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.740
is either on or off.

12
00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:33.630
We write on as one and off as

13
00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:36.150
zero, or say true and false.

14
00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:39.250
A logic gate takes one or two of these

15
00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:41.530
inputs, and gives one output.

16
00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:43.870
Three gates do most of the

17
00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:47.270
work: AND, OR and NOT.

18
00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:51.970
AND is on only when both inputs are on.

19
00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:55.200
Wire two switches one after the

20
00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.740
other, in series, and the lamp

21
00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:00.120
lights only when both are closed.

22
00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:02.990
Hot AND someone in the

23
00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:04.650
room: that's our fan.

24
00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:09.310
OR is on when either input is on, or both.

25
00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:12.840
Wire two switches side by side, in

26
00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:15.680
parallel, and closing either one lights

27
00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:16.100
the lamp.

28
00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:20.280
Two doors, one alarm: front door

29
00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.560
open OR back door open.

30
00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:27.060
NOT flips its input: on becomes

31
00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:29.600
off, and off becomes on.

32
00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:32.150
A fridge light is a NOT.

33
00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:35.350
When the door is shut, it presses the

34
00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:37.010
switch and the light is off.

35
00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.070
Open the door, the switch is no longer

36
00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:41.890
pressed, and the light comes on.

37
00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:43.530
Quick check!

38
00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:46.290
Our school gate opens only if

39
00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:48.630
the guard presses his button AND

40
00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:49.830
a teacher presses hers.

41
00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.700
This morning, only the guard presses.

42
00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:54.590
Does the gate open?

43
00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:56.910
It stays shut.

44
00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:00.840
AND needs both inputs on, so

45
00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:02.340
one button isn't enough.

46
00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:05.190
That's the whole point: two

47
00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:06.030
people must agree.

48
00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:10.280
A truth table lists every combination of

49
00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:12.420
inputs, with the output for each.

50
00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:15.270
Two inputs give four rows.

51
00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:18.650
For AND, only the last row is on.

52
00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:22.130
For OR, only the first row is off.

53
00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:25.470
Real rules combine gates.

54
00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:28.040
A stair light has a switch at the

55
00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:30.640
bottom and one at the top, and

56
00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:31.820
either one changes it.

57
00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.080
It's on when the two switches

58
00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:36.400
differ, a gate called XOR.

59
00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:39.280
A microcontroller runs exactly

60
00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.680
these rules, written in code.

61
00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:43.640
Your turn.

62
00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:48.260
Our water tank alarm beeps if the tank is

63
00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:51.960
nearly empty OR the pump is overheating.

64
00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:55.010
The tank is full, but the

65
00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:56.650
pump is overheating.

66
00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:58.070
Does it beep?

67
00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:03.270
Yes, it beeps: OR needs only one input on.

68
00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:07.790
Remember: AND needs all its inputs, OR

69
00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:10.730
needs any one, and NOT flips.

70
00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:13.680
A truth table checks every case.

71
00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:16.530
Try it in class tomorrow:

72
00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:18.390
human logic gates.

73
00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:22.210
Give pairs of pupils cards with one and

74
00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:25.390
zero, and let a third pupil be the gate.

75
00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:28.480
Then write the fan rule as a

76
00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:29.840
truth table on the board.

77
00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:32.350
Next time: how a device

78
00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:34.290
stores numbers in bits.
